= V1 maturation register =

This register operationalizes [[BITwiki:V1 to V2 maturation]]. It distinguishes historical implementation from design imagination and gives each significant V1 signal a traceable path into V2.

'''A row in this register is not permission to implement a feature.''' It is a commitment to understand the lineage before deciding what V2 should become.

== Status vocabulary ==

* '''Research''' — source lineage and historical behavior are still being reconstructed.
* '''Candidate''' — durable signal is understood and a possible V2 maturation has been identified.
* '''Accepted''' — the maturation direction has been deliberately adopted; implementation or vocabulary coverage may still be incomplete.
* '''Implemented''' — the accepted capability exists and has been validated in V2.
* '''Rejected''' — reviewed but intentionally not carried forward as an active V2 capability.
* '''Historical only''' — preserved for lineage but not intended as an active V2 primitive.

