== Evidence standard ==

Each row should eventually link to an evidence note containing:

# exact V1 archive page and revision identifiers;
# implemented MediaWiki objects and callers/usages where applicable;
# related historical design writings;
# conflicts or changes across revisions;
# current V2 objects addressing the same function;
# explicit rationale for acceptance, rejection, or transformation;
# validation evidence when implemented.

A wanted template, design paragraph, category label, or proposed schema is evidence that an idea existed. It is not evidence that the capability was deployed.

The reusable machine evidence for corpus-level decisions is documented in [[BITwiki:Corpus evidence]] and [[BITwiki:V1 page-role migration]].

== First research passes ==

The register should be matured in an order that reduces downstream ambiguity:

# '''Ontology and classification''' — core primitive separation accepted; corpus inventory and page-role migration complete; subject canonicalization and vocabulary coverage are next.
# '''Epistemics and confidence''' — status, provenance, evidence, uncertainty, review, confidence trails.
# '''Composition''' — Book Matter/transclusion are now Candidates from direct V1 evidence; templates, modules, page anatomy, and caller behavior still require full maturation.
# '''Graph semantics''' — properties, relationships, query behavior, visualization.
# '''Research substrate''' — claims, publications, patents, datasets, methods, experiments, projects, labs, implementations.
# '''Knowledge lifecycle''' — BIThub/BITCORE/artifact/review/canonicalization and reuse.

This ordering is methodological rather than hierarchical. Findings may cross-cut several families.

== Design guardrail ==

'''Do not implement the V1 imagination by recreating the V1 ambiguity.'''

Every accepted maturation should identify:

* the one primary job of each primitive;
* how it composes with other primitives;
* what evidence causes it to exist;
* how its values or behavior are validated;
* how its provenance is preserved;
* whether it is canonical knowledge, navigation, workflow state, generated output, or historical evidence.

